{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"cat docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-probe/reading-rule.md; sed -n '138,182p' src/hivemind/model.py\"","aggregated_output":"# Council Q, round 4: the probe after your round-3 changes (read-only; no edits, no model calls)\n\nYour round 3 (`codex-r3.md`, DISAGREE) asked for four changes. All are taken:\n1. **old-2 only decides.** `probe.py` sends only old-2 (`SEND_DRAWS`): control (the stored 09-20 request of v9, byte-equal) and\n   changed (plus v14's conclusion through one `first_is_bullish` dependency, production's 600-character block), three fresh samples\n   each: 6 sends. old-1 and old-3 are not sent; `render-check.json` records them as examples of what the cut loses.\n2. **Harness.** A sample's archive path that exists refuses the send; both attempts of a refused answer are kept; before each call the\n   worst case (prompt at one token per three characters plus the full 16,000-token output allowance, about $0.011) is reserved against\n   a cap of $0.15.\n3. **The reading rule below, the same for both arms.**\n4. **Use of the linked forecast tracked apart.**\n\n## The reading rule (fixed before any answer)\nFor each answer, two readers (Claude first, then you blind to the arm under shuffled labels, given the answer, v14's 09-20 conclusion\nand the request's evidence) record:\n- **A.** Its FY2027 Data Center estimate and its Q4 FY2027 Data Center estimate, as stated or as its own arithmetic gives them.\n- **B.** Whether its arithmetic adds up (its quarters sum to its year within $2B).\n- **C.** Whether each assumption is disclosed and grounded in the request (a cited figure, guidance, or a stated growth rate from\n  the evidence or from v14's shown conclusion); a step with no source is unsupported.\n- **D.** Room for the rest of NVIDIA: v14's shown figures minus the Data Center figures leave at least $25B for FY2027 and at least\n  $6B for Q4 (the reported non-Data-Center revenue in the request: Q1 $6.35B, Q2 $7.2B, first half $13.55B). Both arms are measured\n  against v14's 09-20 figures ($419B FY, $127B Q4), whether or not the answer saw them.\n- **E.** (changed arm only, apart) whether it uses v14's forecast: cites v14 in `cites_views` or names one of its figures.\n\n**Reconciles** = A gives both figures, B, C and D all hold. A missing Q4 estimate = \"not tested\", never a pass.\n\n- **Pass:** changed reconciles in at least 2 of 3; control reconciles in at most 1 of 3; no added refusal (first attempts compared).\n- **Inconclusive:** control reconciles in 2 or 3 of 3 (the stored contradiction is a coin flip here), or changed has 2 or more\n  \"not tested\".\n- **Fail:** otherwise. A fail says this input did not reliably help; it does not locate the cause.\n- Where the two readers differ on a point, the source decides, both marks recorded.\n\n**What it decides:** pass → reopen the dependency design review (D542's five items, the `reads`/`supports` separation, D538's seven\nfiling changes) with the council, then Alex; fail or inconclusive → report to Alex, no further send without a new design.\n\nIs this now sound to send? End with CONSENSUS or DISAGREE. Under 250 words.\n        raise ValueError('max_attempts must be a positive integer')\n    for attempt in range(max_attempts):\n        try:\n            with urllib.request.urlopen(urllib.request.Request(url, data=body, headers=headers, method='POST'), timeout=timeout) as response:\n                raw_bytes = response.read()\n                try:\n                    raw = raw_bytes.decode('utf-8')\n                except UnicodeDecodeError:\n                    if max_attempts != 1:\n                        raise\n                    failure = TransportError('invalid UTF-8 HTTP response')\n                    failure.response_body = raw_bytes.decode('utf-8', 'replace')\n                    failure.response_body_base64 = base64.b64encode(raw_bytes).decode('ascii')\n                    failure.http_status = response.status\n                    raise failure\n                try:\n                    return json.loads(raw)\n                except json.JSONDecodeError:\n                    if max_attempts != 1:\n                        raise\n                    failure = TransportError('malformed HTTP response')\n                    failure.response_body = raw\n                    failure.http_status = response.status\n                    raise failure\n        except urllib.error.HTTPError as error:\n            body_bytes = error.read()\n            body_text = body_bytes.decode('utf-8', 'replace' if max_attempts == 1 else 'ignore')\n            last_http = (error.code, body_text, base64.b64encode(body_bytes).decode('ascii'))\n            last = f'HTTP {error.code}: {body_text[:600]}'\n            if error.code in (400, 401, 403, 404):\n                failure = TransportError(last)\n                failure.response_body = body_text\n                failure.response_body_base64 = last_http[2]\n                failure.http_status = error.code\n                raise failure\n        except (urllib.error.URLError, TimeoutError, ConnectionError, OSError, http.client.HTTPException) as error:   # a dropped or truncated response is retried like a network error\n            last = repr(error)[:200]\n            last_http = None   # the final failure describes the last attempt only\n        if max_attempts == 3 or attempt + 1 < max_attempts:\n            time.sleep(5 * (attempt + 1))\n    failure = TransportError(last or 'no answer')\n    if last_http:\n        failure.http_status, failure.response_body, failure.response_body_base64 = last_http\n    raise failure\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
