{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"sqlite3 -readonly poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-2/prod/views.sqlite \\\"select view_id, call_id, implied_outcome from judgements where view_id in ('v9','v14') and publication_day='2026-09-20' order by judgement_id;\\\"; rg -n 'Q3|incurred|token' docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-probe/render-check.json\"","aggregated_output":"v14|8729|About $419 billion: Q1 $81.6 billion plus Q2 $96.2 billion, estimated Q3 of about $113.5 billion (the $110.16 billion guidance high end plus the reported average 3.1% beat), and Q4 of about $127 billion by carrying forward the guided 12% sequential growth.\nv9|8737|Approximately $410 billion: $164 billion reported in the first half, about $100 billion implied for Q3 from the $108 billion total-revenue guide and recent Data Center mix, and roughly $146 billion estimated for Q4. The Q4 estimate reflects management's expected hyperscale reacceleration and Rubin ramp, with a discounted contribution from SemiAnalysis's forecast that second-half Data Center revenue would exceed analyst estimates by 20%.\n17:  \"shown\": \"- v14 (open; first_is_bullish) How much total revenue will NVIDIA report for FY2027?: now rung 2 Bullish; reasons: The reference is about $411 billion for FY2027, which sits at rung 2; the cited Zacks growth estimate also implies about $405 billion using FY2026 revenue of $215.9 billion. The operating run-rate implies about $419 billion: estimate Q3 at roughly $113.5 billion by applying the cited average 3.1% beat to the $110.16 billion high end of guidance, then carry the guided 12% sequential growth forward to Q4, about $127 billion, alongside reported Q1 and Q2 revenue. Supply constraints are a meaningful downside risk, but the cited estimate of more than $100 billion in unfulfilled demand is for “next\",\n26:  \"shown\": \"- v3 (open; first_is_bullish) What will NVIDIA report as total revenue for FY2027?: now rung 1 Strongly bullish; reasons: The market reference is about $411 billion (e4360, e5406), which sits in rung 2 ($392 billion to below $431.2 billion). The evidence-based run-rate is about $419 billion before the additional second-half data-center-compute uplift: first-half revenue was $177.837 billion; Q3 is about $113.6 billion using the $108 billion midpoint guidance and the cited 3.1% average beat over the high end; carrying the guided 12% sequential growth pace forward gives about $127 billion for Q4. Applying SemiAnalysis’s 20% uplift only to second-half data-center compute adds about $27–28 billion, implying roughly $\",\n27:  \"cut_off\": \"446 billion and crossing the rung-1 boundary. The analyst view of 90% Q3 and 65% Q4 year-over-year growth is a counter-signal, but it does not outweigh the guided-growth run-rate and the specific second-half compute tracking. The 70% full-year growth statement would imply about $367 billion from FY2026 revenue, but that would require a sharp Q4 decline after the reported first half and Q3 guidance, so it is inconsistent with the nearer-term run-rate.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"agent_message","text":"**Almost. Check Q3 as well before sending.** With $164.25B in the first half, $120B in Q3 and $100B in Q4, Data Center totals $384.25B. That clears both proposed floors even though Q3 Data Center exceeds v14’s $113.5B for all of NVIDIA. Record Q3 under A and require it to fit under the same company-wide forecast under D. Keep the $25B and $6B floors as explicit assumptions for this test. [Reading rule](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-probe/reading-rule.md)\n\nUse v14 as the same comparison point for both arms. For C, give an answer credit only for support its own request contained. Record whether a linked figure actually bounds or changes the calculation under E. A citation alone shows the answer noticed the link.\n\nThe harness now rejects existing sample archives and retains both attempts after a judgement refusal. One token per three characters is an estimate. For a hard $0.15 cap, reserve against the full request’s token bound and disable or budget the transport’s automatic retries. [Probe script](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-probe/probe.py:91) · [Transport](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/model.py:131)\n\nWith those changes, six sends are enough for the narrow decision to reopen design review. They leave production readiness open.\n\n**DISAGREE**"}}
